      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "In 1850, the state legislature founded the Carolina Female College in Ansonville, a school for daughters of local planters that served only white women.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ansonville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The college closed during the Civil War, with sources citing either 1862 or 1867 as the year of its shutdown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ansonville%2C_North_Carolina",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ansonville lies on the northern edge of Anson County, just a mile west of the Pee Dee River.",
